# Metric Key Naming Convention

All metric keys in `EvalResult.metrics` follow this prefix scheme:

| Prefix | Category | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `label_reg_` | Supervised regression on parameter_0 | `label_reg_emb_r2`, `label_reg_improvement_r2` |
| `comp_cluster_` | Component clustering metrics | `comp_cluster_ari`, `comp_cluster_nmi` |
| `comp_knn_` | Component KNN/neighbor metrics | `comp_knn_precision_k10` |
| `repr_` | Representation geometry | `repr_cka_linear`, `repr_uniformity` |
| `spectral_` | Spectral-domain metrics | `spectral_reconstruction_snr` |
| `downstream_` | Downstream task results | `downstream_linear_probe_r2` |
| `noise_` | Noise robustness metrics | `noise_gaussian_robustness_ratio` |
| `stack_` | Stack/similarity metrics | `stack_match_improvement_pct` |
| `completion_` | Signal completion | `completion_score` |
| `eval_` | Validation loss | `eval_loss` |

## Rules
1. Snake_case only: `label_reg_emb_r2` not `labelRegEmbR2`
2. Space names in multi-space metrics: `label_reg_emb_r2` vs `label_reg_input_r2`
3. Improvement metrics: `*_improvement_*` means emb-space minus input-space
4. Every key MUST have a description in `metric_descriptions` dict of `EvalResult`
5. Every eval method MUST register at least one plot in `plot_paths`
